  "notes": "Four weeks at R8 000 (2, 9, 16, 23 March 2026), then the first fortnight (30 March - 12 April) at R16 000: the same R416 000 a year. G21 (2027) Rev 1 p. 8-9 (Fourth Schedule para 9(1)/(2)): AE = remuneration x periods in the year / periods worked, tax x periods worked / periods in the year. SARS does not say how to count periods across a change of pay period, so the four weeks are counted as the share of a year they are, 4 / 52, in fortnights: 4 x 26 / 52 = 2 (UNVERIFIED). n = 2 + 1 = 3; YTD 48 000; AE = 48 000 x 26 / 3 = 416 000; tax(416 000) = 79 998 + 31% x 32 900 - 17 820 = 72 377; liability 72 377 x 3 / 26 = 8 351.19; less 4 x 1 391.87 (each week's tables PAYE, 72 377 / 52) = 2 783.71. Counting the weeks as fortnights (n = 5) gave AE 249 600 and nil. Each prior's UIF is 1% capped at the March ceiling of 177.12 across the month's runs (not asserted). expectedWarnings: PAY_FREQUENCY_CHANGED_IN_YEAR, the conversion's visible UNVERIFIED caution.",
